  "SC2130": {
    "code": "SC2130",
    "title": "`-eq` is for integer comparisons. Use `=` instead.",
    "fix": "`-eq` is for integer comparisons. Use `=` instead.",
    "rationale": "Shells have two sets of comparison operators: for integers (`-eq`, `-gt`, ...) and strings (`=`, `>`, ...). ShellCheck has noticed that you're using an integer comparison with string data.\n\nIf you are in fact comparing integers, double check your parameters. Certain mistakes like `$$foo` or `${bar}}` can introduce non-numeric characters into otherwise numeric arguments.",
