    "code": "SC2143",
    "title": "Use `grep -q` instead of comparing output with `[ -n .. ]`.",
    "fix": "Use `grep -q` instead of comparing output with `[ -n .. ]`.",
    "rationale": "The problematic code has to iterate the entire directory and read all matching lines into memory before making a decision.\n\nThe correct code is cleaner and stops at the first matching line, avoiding both iterating the rest of the directory and reading data into memory.",
    "problematicCode": "if [ -n \"$(find . | grep 'IMG[0-9]')\" ]\nthen\n  echo \"Images found\"\nfi",
