    "fix": "Use `-n` instead of `! -z`.",
    "rationale": "You have negated `test -z` or `test -n`, resulting in a needless double-negative. You can just use the other operator instead:\n\n```sh\n# Identical tests to verify that a value is assigned\n[ ! -z foo ] # Not has no value\n[ -n foo ]   # Has value\n\n# Identical tests to verify that a value is empty\n[ ! -n foo ] # Not is non-empty\n[ -z foo ]   # Is empty\n```",
