    "rationale": "`$\"..\"` is a localized string, for example, `echo $\"Hello $USER\"` along with the proper translation files can be used to have the script say \"Bonjour, youruser\" in French locales.\n\nIn this case, ShellCheck found a localized string whose contents is also the name of a variable. This could have happened because the user wanted a far more common quoted substitution, e.g. `\"$var\"`, but accidentally switched the leading `$` and `\"`.",
